## Summary

This PR adds an operational overview endpoint to the admin workload module.

It introduces:

- `GET /admin/workload/overview`

The endpoint aggregates existing workload signals into a manager-friendly operational dashboard response.

## Business / Ops purpose

Lots 179 to 184 introduced:

- admin ownership and SLA tracking;
- admin timeline events;
- workload queues;
- workload actions;
- workload urgency signals;
- workload review visibility.

This PR adds a consolidated overview so admins and ops managers can quickly understand overall pressure and risk across the workload.

The overview answers questions such as:

- how many workload items are open;
- how many are critical or high urgency;
- how many are overdue or due soon;
- how many need review attention;
- how many have recent admin action;
- which object types are most represented;
- which SLA statuses and recommended actions dominate;
- which assignees carry the highest workload/risk.

## Main changes

- Add `AdminWorkloadOverviewResponseDto`.
- Add `GET /admin/workload/overview`.
- Add `AdminWorkloadService.getOverview`.
- Aggregate workload items by:
  - object type;
  - operational status;
  - urgency level;
  - SLA status;
  - recommended action.
- Add top assignee workload/risk distribution.
- Extend controller and service tests.

## Non-goals

This PR does not:

- add a new database table;
- add a Prisma migration;
- change AdminOwnership persistence;
- change AdminTimeline persistence;
- change AdminActionAudit persistence;
- introduce auto-assignment;
- introduce notifications;
- change dispute, payout, refund, AML, trust, reconciliation or financial-control business rules;
- add frontend behavior.

## Validation

- `npm test -- src/admin-workload/admin-workload.service.spec.ts src/admin-workload/admin-workload.controller.spec.ts`
- `npm run build`
